  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Drylands - CEA Grootvlei</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Drylands Farms B.V. is a Dutch-owned agricultural technology company committed to developing scalable, climate-resilient greenhouse farming solutions tailored to the African context. Drylands leverages Dutch expertise in Controlled Environment Agriculture (CEA) to address food security and employment challenges in rapidly urbanizing regions. The Grootvlei CEA project, located in South Africa, is a flagship initiative under the Dutch combi-track supporting the Just Energy Transition (JET). It aims to repurpose the Grootvlei coal power station into a sustainable agricultural hub. The project begins with a 0.5-hectare proof-of-concept pilot, supported by Dutch industry partners and the Dutch Embassy in Pretoria, and is designed to scale to 15-100 hectares. Invest International has approved a EUR 700,000 development contribution: EUR 370,000 as a non-repayable development contribution for climate upgrades and EUR 330,000 as a repayable contribution contingent on successful commercial expansion.</narrative>
  </description>
